The first key correction is already clear from Apple’s own docs: `.playback` plus the `audio` background mode is explicitly designed to continue through screen lock, and Apple documents continuous looping on `AVAudioPlayer`. A pre-started silence-then-beep asset therefore avoids deadline scheduling in exactly the way you describe. I’m checking the project’s actual attempt next, because ownership/session-lifecycle bugs are more plausible than a “too quiet” threshold.
